<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine data points to deflation in March.</title>
<headline>Argentine data points to deflation in March.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Early Argentine data suggests that consumer prices are falling in March and that the overall index will decline, the economy minister's chief aide said Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;Deflation in the month was to be expected as there was a rise in January due to tourism while in March this sector typically falls,&quot; Carlos Rodriguez told reporters.  </p>
<p>Inflation in February was 0.4 percent. The consumer price index fell 0.5 percent in March 1996.</p>
<p>((Gary Regenstreif, Buenos Aires newsroom, 541 3180618))</p>
